{"id": "EUVD-2026-108909", "enisaUuid": "eafd58f1-c39d-3e46-ba4c-aea11dfc7cbc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nperf/core: Check kernel access when kernel callchains are requested\n\nperf_event_open() currently gates perf_allow_kernel() only on\n!attr.exclude_kernel.\n\nHowever, users can still request kernel callchain collection with\nattr.exclude_callchain_kernel == 0 even when attr.exclude_kernel == 1.\nThat still requires kernel profiling privilege, but the existing check\ndoes not enforce it.\n\nUpdate the permission check to call perf_allow_kernel() when either\nkernel sampling is requested or kernel callchains are requested.\n\nThis keeps permission checks aligned with requested data and prevents\nunprivileged use of kernel callchain capture.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:11:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:11:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/132bee76097be421ab3012130b5b506324cf2be1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2581b43e162cfc43e6f5d8dd8d2b38f3441550de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e187281f978a2bff98ead6aa40f8ddc9a2c9afb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4573a3838ae4fc73b70019cfa1dac9aaea7cc2f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98937"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "204ef8b6-896f-3ae8-8873-cd0f5d40aa40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5d7ed08e-c00d-395d-94e8-d14d8e65a2b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2581b43e162cfc43e6f5d8dd8d2b38f3441550de"}, {"id": "6449f1b2-a5b1-316d-aaa8-5a616a001e38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "81604961-e7f7-3f5e-82dd-424a2c6ac5d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.18.56"}, {"id": "b083127b-65dc-3833-868c-f4d6079f478e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.113"}, {"id": "cac3102c-5886-3fb5-ae19-fde808ff6249", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <6e187281f978a2bff98ead6aa40f8ddc9a2c9afb"}, {"id": "cb2c7fcd-2204-334a-b3ac-af15bc98424d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <a4573a3838ae4fc73b70019cfa1dac9aaea7cc2f"}, {"id": "d3a9e4aa-0e92-3f26-adb1-7fb183034e4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "da8f9f21-1e14-3d76-ae51-876e1eecbbc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <7.2.10"}, {"id": "dc29ee11-db0e-30fa-a7d3-775427c35a2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "dce815f7-092c-3f48-9799-8826ded8e7f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <132bee76097be421ab3012130b5b506324cf2be1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7f8f9d5b-5544-34c0-a3ff-5285680c460f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}